"""T0 launch-timing fixture: terminal enter/restore with no widgets.

Workload T0 of the slim-UI benchmark design (section 8.1): "initialize/restore
terminal, no widgets" -- it isolates terminal-provider initialization overhead
from the H0 runtime/loader floor and from T1's parse+render+input work.

Deliberately emits the alternate-screen and cursor sequences LITERALLY rather
than importing an ANSI helper: T0 must not drag any `app.ui`/`common.ui` module
into its import closure, or it stops being a provider-initialization floor and
becomes a second T1. The sequences match `run_tui_stub`
(`src/app/ui.tui/app.spl`) byte for byte.

Driven by `scripts/check/check-ui-slim-startup.shs --lane T0`, which asserts the
marker line below appears on stdout; a run without it is a FAIL, not a sample.
"""

fn main():
    print "\x1b[?1049h"
    print "\x1b[?25l"
    print "ui-slim-t0-altscreen"
    print "\x1b[?25h"
    print "\x1b[?1049l"
